  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation is\r\n$$\r\n\\left(1+x^{2}\\right) \\frac{d y}{d x}+y=e^{\\tan ^{-1} x}\r\n$$\r\nor it can be rewritten as\r\n$$\r\n\\frac{d y}{d x}+\\frac{1}{\\left(1+x^{2}\\right)} y=\\frac{e^{\\tan ^{-1} x}}{1+x^{2}}\r\n$$\r\nIt is a linear differential equation of the form of\r\n$$\r\n\\frac{d y}{d x}+P y=Q\r\n$$\r\nwhere, $P=\\frac{1}{1+x^{2}}$ and $Q=\\frac{e^{\\tan ^{-1} x}}{1+x^{2}}$\r\n$$\r\n=e^{\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^{2}} d x}=e^{\\tan ^{-1} x}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
